Let rows be 3.
Let columns be 7.
Let size be the product of rows and columns.
Let table be a list of size zeros.
For every position from 0 to one less than size.
Let row be position divided by columns.
Let column be position modulo columns.
If row is 0 or column is 0, set item position of table to 1.
If row is more than 0 and column is more than 0, set item position of table to item (position minus columns) of table plus item (position minus 1) of table.


Let last be one less than size.
Print item last of table.
